1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,980
How does an order service

2
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:02,707
get its payment gateway?

3
00:00:02,887 --> 00:00:04,240
Require a payment gateway

4
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:05,340
in the constructor,

5
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:08,298
and keep its reference in a final field.

6
00:00:08,518 --> 00:00:10,460
Boot scans the components.

7
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,680
One gateway bean matches

8
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,334
that interface type.

9
00:00:13,554 --> 00:00:14,820
Spring passes it into

10
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,080
the service constructor

11
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:19,020
before the application places an order.

12
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:21,820
Our Boot test confirms the same bean.

13
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:22,960
A fake gateway passes

14
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,973
a separate service test.

15
00:00:25,193 --> 00:00:27,660
Require, resolve, inject, then use.

16
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:29,660
Constructor injection makes

17
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:32,283
required dependencies explicit.

18
00:00:34,283 --> 00:00:35,469
Thanks for watching.

